@xumi0920/dsh-browser-harness README · 快速开始：安装生效后，先启动专用 Chromium 浏览器（默认 9331），然后在**任意 DSH 会话**里让模型调用（所有预设可用，创造模式只影响 `plugin_manager` 安装）：

```
browser_status → browser_navigate {url} → browser_snapshot → browser_act {action:"click", ref}
browser_extract {mode:"text" | "html" | "js" | "network" | "console" | "frames"}
```

首调 `connected:false`？确认专用浏览器已启动且 `http://127.0.0.1:9331/json/version` 可访问（见 [docs/configuration.md](docs/configuration.md)）。

@xumi0920/dsh-browser-harness README · 扩展与语言：- **原生插件**：Node 22+ ESM 包（JS/TS，TS 需构建），bundle patch 注册，HMR 协调热插拔。
- **其它语言**：写 MCP server（stdio / Streamable HTTP，Python / Go / Rust / Node 均可），profile 里加 `@deepseek-ai/dsh-mcp-client`，工具以 `mcp__<serverName>__<tool>` 暴露。
- **技能**：Markdown（`SKILL.md`）；**UI 插件**：JS/TS。细节见 [docs/extending.md](docs/extending.md)。

@xumi0920/dsh-browser-harness README · Install：1. **Plugins page (recommended)**: DSH Web → Plugins → Add plugin → Install a third-party plugin. Accepts npm package names, Git repositories and local directories; marketplace entries live under the **Discover** tab.
2. **Ask DSH in one sentence** (Creator-mode session): `Install @xumi0920/dsh-browser-harness into the current profile`.
3. **Manual install (GitHub Packages, classic PAT)**:

@xumi0920/dsh-browser-harness README · Quick start：Once the install is live, start the dedicated Chromium browser (default 9331), then let the model call the tools in **any DSH session** (all presets work; Creator mode only matters for the `plugin_manager` install step):

```
browser_status → browser_navigate {url} → browser_snapshot → browser_act {action:"click", ref}
browser_extract {mode:"text" | "html" | "js" | "network" | "console" | "frames"}
```

@xumi0920/dsh-browser-harness README · Extending & languages：- **Native plugins:** Node 22+ ESM packages (JS/TS, TS needs a build) registered through a bundle patch; HMR coordinates hot-plugging.
- **Other languages:** write an MCP server (stdio / Streamable HTTP; Python / Go / Rust / Node all work), add a `@deepseek-ai/dsh-mcp-client` entry to the profile, and its tools appear as `mcp__<serverName>__<tool>`.
- **Skills:** Markdown (`SKILL.md`); **UI plugins:** JS/TS. Details: [docs/extending.md](docs/extending.md).
